{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>The one lamb.</b> It should have said האחד (the one), but it comes to allude that they were occupied with the daily offering in thirteen, which is the numerical value of אחד; therefore it says את הכבש אחד to allude 'the lamb of אחד' — that is, for the name of HaShem who is One. And in the section ואתה תצוה (Exodus 29:39) it says את הכבש האחד, the singular one of the flock." "<b>You shall prepare in the morning.</b> It is by gematria לארבע שעות (four hours), for thus testified R. Yehudah ben Bava concerning the morning daily offering, that it was offered at four hours." "<b>In the morning.</b> From when the sun's radiance begins to spread its shining throughout the world, because the world was created on a day, as it is said (Genesis 2:4): ״ביום עשות ה׳ אלהים ארץ ושמים״."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {2 "Reading משתנץ as a form of משתנץ/משתנה (begins to change/radiate); the word is textually unusual and the translation follows the context of dawn light spreading."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:40.649568883Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}